#
#	aarch64-specific files
#
#	No hand-written atomics needed here the way riscv64's
#	ainc-riscv64.$O is: os/inferno/virtarm64/archvirtarm64.c defines
#	ainc()/adec() directly in C (spl-masked, MAXMACH==1), the same
#	shape armv7's own archv7.c already uses -- copied from there
#	verbatim.  Everything else is the portable, correct-and-slow C,
#	same choice riscv64/virt's own mkfile-riscv64 makes.
#
#	getfcr-arm64.$O is the exception, and it has to be assembly:
#	FPCR and FPSR are system registers and the compiler has no word
#	for one.  Without it libmath's FPinit() has no setfcr to call
#	and no aarch64 board can carry the built-in $Math module.
#
TARGFILES=\
	frexp-386.$O\
	getfcr-arm64.$O\
	memmove.$O\
	memset.$O\
	nan-386.$O\
	strchr.$O\
